<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- THE PLATFORM THEME EVERY KAYA APP DECLARES, and the reason it
         exists is a measured half-dark-mode (docs/styling-plan.md D1).

         An Activity's window background, its status bar and everything
         drawn before the first Compose frame come from the MANIFEST
         theme, which no Compose theme reaches. Every kaya app used to
         name `@android:style/Theme.Material.Light*` — a hard LIGHT
         theme — so a composition following the system into dark mode
         put dark-scheme controls on a light page: screencapped on
         emulator-5554, window #FAFAFA in both appearances while the
         primary role moved #6750A4 -> #D0BCFF.

         DAY/NIGHT WITHOUT APPCOMPAT: the `-night` resource qualifier
         does it, which is the platform's own mechanism and needs no
         dependency (AppCompat's DayNight themes are the same trick with
         a compatibility layer for the pre-API-29 devices that had no
         system dark mode; kaya's floor is API 26 and those devices
         simply stay light, which is exactly what `isSystemInDarkTheme()`
         reports there).

         ONE entry, NoActionBar, for every validation app since
         2026-08-19: kaya's Compose backend draws the whole chrome
         surface, so a platform action bar above it is double chrome no
         kaya app ships — and it shifts every window-space rectangle
         the ranges pixel witness aims its photograph with, which is
         how the divergence was found (ranges-jvm/-go, the day both
         suites first ran the scene). -->
    <style name="Theme.Kaya.NoActionBar"
        parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
